{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Behold.</b> The prophet now returns to further reprove the people of the exile, and at the end he says, \"And this is My covenant,\" and all the pericopes are connected." "And the sense of <b>Behold, it is not too short</b>: know that HaShem's hand is not too short to save you."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 59, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:11.510760361Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}